# 0.3.31 (V5-14): interrupted-swap residue and staging `next` dirs — a failed
# or re-run prepare-release leaves multi-MB dirs a bare `git add -A` would commit.
dist.previous/
dist.next/
.release-staging.previous/
.release-staging.next/
/files/
# G0/0.7 review fix (2026-10-15): the bed manifest is a SHIPPED artifact (an in-register deliverable),
# but the `files/` rule above ignored it, so a fresh CI checkout had no manifest at all and
# `gen-line-manifest --check` reported stale on a tree nobody had touched. Un-ignore the ONE file;
# the rule above stays as it is (tightening it is a separate repo-hygiene item). Anchoring is the load-bearing half: git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded, so `files/` had to become `/files/` (root only) for this line to mean anything.
!packages/scripts/files/line-manifest.json

# Local scratch and generated parity output (never publish or commit).
/tmp-session.jsonl
/undefined/
packages/evolution-merge-engine/vendor/out/
# W7.2 (2026-11-11): `D:/dsh/_tools/setup-mirror-tests.mjs` writes these two at the mirror root so a
# single-package `tsc`/`vitest` resolves the platform line. They are MACHINE wiring, not repo content —
# and the same script's platform junctions must never be captured by a bare `git add -A` either: it now
# appends their names to `.git/info/exclude` (a checkout-shared ignore would have to blacklist 22
# platform group names at two depths), and verify-package-map fails the release gate when they exist.
/tsconfig.mirror.json
/vitest.mirror.config.ts

